   :two-further-findings-measured-not-asserted
   ["THE TYPED ABSENCE MACHINERY HAS THREE PRODUCTION INHABITANTS AND ITS REFUSAL BRANCH HAS NONE. AC1's C130 2 ruling gave R3a a three-status producer, and over 889 records in 57 files it has emitted :absent exactly three times: three records in data/wm-trace/wm-trace-2026-09-02.edn, each carrying one :prediction-triple-events entry {:producer-contract :prediction-error/v1, :channel :sorry-count-norm, :status :absent, :absent-member :observed, :reason :source-field-missing, :paths [[:graph :summary :total-sorrys]]}, and :prediction-triple-omitted 1 at each of its three micro-steps. The correspondence is exact and total -- the three records with seven channels ARE the three records with a triple event. :prediction-triple-refused appears on no record of the 889, so the caller's refusal rule at war_machine.clj:6116-6128, which the harness verifies works, has never run in production. The coverage distribution is therefore NOT a two-era ascent: {0 2, 1 2, 4 127, 6 17, 8 738, 7 3}, and the 7 is the LATEST era's, three records on 2026-09-02 sitting between 8-channel records on either side, not an earlier rung."
    "R3a's BELIEVE PLACEMENT RESTS ON A CLAIM WITH 878 OF 878 WITNESSES. The basis argues the node belongs in BELIEVE because it reads the belief and re-runs as that belief moves. That is a code reading; the corpus makes it a measurement. 878 records carry a micro-step trace, every one of them runs exactly three steps, and in every one of the 878 the terminal :error-magnitude differs from step 0's -- signed change from -0.010355815188529793 to +0.0012330139293520448, 828 decreased and 50 INCREASED, the increases confined to five files (2026-07-17, 07-18, 08-30, 08-31, 09-01). So the projection demonstrably re-runs against a moved belief in every record that could show it. THE SAME NUMBER RECORDS A SECOND THING: all 878 ran the full three steps, so neither of the loop's other two exits -- the refusal exit and the `error-mag < r3-error-eps` convergence exit (war_machine.clj:6225-6227) -- has ever fired. And what the trace persists as :prediction-errors is the TERMINAL step's weighted errors -- the map is returned at war_machine.clj:6230, inside the branch the loop takes only when it exits (war_machine.clj:6225-6227), so terminality follows from the loop's structure. STATED PRECISELY BECAUSE THE NEARBY COMMENT IS ABOUT A DIFFERENT KEY: the 'This is the TERMINAL step's records' comment at war_machine.clj:6232-6236 annotates the sibling :prediction-triple-events stream at :6237, not :prediction-errors. On all 878 records the persisted map is therefore not the projection that drove the first belief event."]

